# Case: Independent native Desktop windows and process lifetimes
# Mode: native
# Purpose: Verify independent GUI, quick-panel, tray and service processes through native windows with an isolated directory clipboard.
# Steps:
#   Record role identities; request the panel through tray IPC; copy real service history through the native panel; close the GUI process; reopen it through tray IPC and inspect the new process and window.
# Expected:
#   Every role has a distinct PID; panel Copy writes exact directory-board bytes; standby has no windows while the PID survives; reopening renders fresh history and satellite; GUI close terminates its process; tray and service remain; tray IPC creates a new native GUI process with retained history.
# Forbidden:
#   System clipboard access, physical input, native tray-click claims, global shortcut claims, hidden resident GUI, shared role PIDs, missing screenshots or missing continuous sampled-window recording.

start
submit native-role-content 'Desktop independent native process copy'
ui-wait listItem 'Desktop independent native process copy'
role-checkpoint started
screenshot main-started
role-panel-hidden
role-open-panel
ui-wait button '历史：Desktop independent native process copy'
ui-set textField '搜索快捷面板' 'independent native'
ui-wait button '历史：Desktop independent native process copy'
role-panel-preview
screenshot independent-panel
role-panel-copy
board-equals 'Desktop independent native process copy'
role-panel-hidden
submit native-role-standby 'New independent native entry from standby'
role-open-panel
ui-wait button '历史：Desktop independent native process copy'
ui-wait button '历史：New independent native entry from standby'
role-panel-query 'independent native'
role-panel-preview
screenshot recreated-panel
role-panel-copy
board-equals 'Desktop independent native process copy'
role-select-gui
screenshot panel-copy-applied
role-close-gui
role-reopen-gui
ui-wait listItem 'Desktop independent native process copy'
screenshot recreated-gui
